<title>GERMANY: Porsche dismisses BW Bank forecast.</title>
<headline>Porsche dismisses BW Bank forecast.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>German sports car maker Porsche AG on Wednesday dismissed a statment by Baden-Wuerttembergische Bank AG that the carmaker told its analysts it expected sales of 3.6 billion marks and profit of over 100 million marks this year.</p>
<p>A Porsche spokesman said the company would not make any forecast on sales or earnings for the business year that is set to end on July 31.</p>
<p>Earlier the BW Bank quoted Porsche chief finance officer Holger Haerter as giving the sales and profit forecasts to analysts at a seminar.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
